dsv41 patch 0067 (21.10.2026): a shorter eager "vor" phase (the kernels between the drafter graph and the target graph
of a decode round): the decode SWA metadata of all sliding-window groups in one launch. In use (VLLM_DSV41_VOR_FUSED=1,
image v18 and later; measured with 0066's VLLM_DSV41_MARKOV_FUSED=1). Base: vllm/v1/attention/backends/mla/sparse_swa.py
as in the recipe image (no patch of ours touches it) and vllm/models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/model_state.py of image v12;
new file vllm/models/deepseek_v41/common/ops/swa_fused.py.
Why: between the drafter graph and the target graph every round runs ~103 eager kernels on the main stream, 0.27 ms of
GPU time (profile of 19.10., 1 stream; the host is ~30 ms ahead, so all of it is on the GPU's critical path). 94 us of
it is the SWA metadata: build_attn_metadata calls DeepseekSparseSWAMetadataBuilder.build once per sliding-window KV
cache group (15 on DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash: 43 SWA layers, 3 a group), and each runs torch.ge(slot_mapping, 0),
decode_swa_lens[n:] = 0 and _compute_swa_indices_and_lens_kernel: 45 launches of 1-3 us with ~0.5 us gaps. Another
9 us: the model state uploads replay_start every round (16 B pinned -> device), zeros in decode-only rounds.
How:
  1. swa (VLLM_DSV41_VOR_FUSED=1 or =swa): model_state.prepare_attn arms a plan with every KV group whose only attention
     group has a DeepseekSparseSWAMetadataBuilder (in build order, with the block tables and slot-mapping rows that
     build_attn_metadata hands them). The first of these builders launches _swa_decode_groups_kernel once for all
     groups (a per-group row of a cached int64 pointer table): rows < n run torch.ge for the token and then the
     upstream kernel's body verbatim, tail programs the torch.ge of the slot-mapping entries past n and
     decode_swa_lens[n:] = 0. The other builders skip their three launches if their inputs are the ones the launch
     read. Only decode-only causal steps; mixed steps, captures, microbatches, the drafter's builders and any mismatch
     take the upstream path unchanged.
  2. copy (=1 or =copy): the replay_start upload runs only when the values differ from what the device buffer holds
     (the model state is its only writer).
Same bits: the same values land in the same buffers, the metadata objects are unchanged and the graphs read the same
addresses. Tested on CPU (a numpy interpreter of the Triton subset: 34 decode steps x 15 groups incl. FULL padding,
contexts up to 327K, replay starts, stale buffers; mismatch / mixed / non-causal fallbacks; five mutated kernels are
all caught) and on GB10 (sm_121, bits ok). Expected from the profile: -0.09 ms (swa) and -0.008 ms (copy) of GPU time a
round, ~-0.3 %, below what an A/B of tok/s resolves.
Measured (21.10.2026, GB10, 2000 MHz, image v18, from a fresh start): together with 0066's MARKOV_FUSED against the
stored reference run of the production setup without both: cost per verify round -0.66 % (geometric mean), T=0 texts
identical (details in 0066). Not measured alone.
Switch: VLLM_DSV41_VOR_FUSED=1 (both parts), =swa, =copy; default 0 = off (the base image's kernels and buffers).

